The function `media_request_ioctl_reinit()` ran without holding `mdev->req_queue_mutex`, which was already used to serialize request queueing with STREAMON/OFF. Meanwhile, `VIDIOC_REQBUFS(0)` could tear down the vb2 queue concurrently, leading to a race condition where request object cleanup and queue cancellation happen in parallel. This could cause use-after-free when a request object is freed while still being accessed by the queue teardown path.

