The fix acquires `mdev->req_queue_mutex` at the start of `media_request_ioctl_reinit()` and releases it after all state transitions and cleanup are complete. This ensures that `REINIT` is serialized with `REQBUFS(0)` (which also now takes the same mutex) and with other request operations that use `req_queue_mutex`. The mutual exclusion prevents concurrent request cleanup and queue teardown, eliminating the race condition and the associated use-after-free vulnerability.

